{"name":"Wax Crayon Blue","hex":"#00a4a6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wax","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Watam."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any oily, water-resistant, solid or semisolid substance; normally long-chain hydrocarbons, alcohols or esters.","Beeswax (a wax secreted by bees)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wax"},{"term":"crayon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stick of colored chalk or wax used for drawing.","A colored pencil, a colouring pencil"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To draw with a crayon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crayon"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crayon","blocks":[{"text":"A crayon is a stick of pigmented wax used for writing or drawing. Wax crayons differ from pastels, in which the pigment is mixed with a dry binder such as gum arabic, and from oil pastels, where the binder is a mixture of wax and oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Crayones_cera.jpg/330px-Crayones_cera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crayon","wikidata":"Q69158"},{"title":"Wax","blocks":[{"text":"Waxes are a diverse class of organic compounds that are lipophilic solids that are malleable near ambient temperatures. They include higher alkanes and lipids, typically with melting points above about 40 °C (104 °F), melting to give low viscosity liquids. Waxes are insoluble in water but soluble in nonpolar organic solvents such as hexane, benzene and chloroform. Natural waxes of various types are produced by plants and animals and occur in petroleum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Beeswax_foundation.jpg/330px-Beeswax_foundation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wax","wikidata":"Q124695"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/VariousCrayonBoxes.jpg/500px-VariousCrayonBoxes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/VariousCrayonBoxes.jpg/500px-VariousCrayonBoxes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wide variety of crayon boxes have been produced over the years.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVariousCrayonBoxes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Dixon_Crayon_Ad.jpg/500px-Dixon_Crayon_Ad.jpg?utm_source